ker.conf with nofile=8192 and nproc=256, verified via real login shells enforcing pam_limits both before and after a single acknowledged reboot on node1. The provider-wide restart-evidence protocol was also satisfied for node1: a healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id f9bf293d...), a returned reboot acknowledgement, a differing post-restart boot_id (38b52693...) matching the fixed after-executor snapshot, and recovered account/limits state were all directly observed.\",\"limitations\":[\"The single-node topology means the restart protocol was only exercised on node1; no cross-node comparison was possible or needed.\",\"The first ulimit -u check used sh instead of bash and failed with an unrelated shell syntax error, requiring a follow-up command to get a valid nproc reading; this did not affect the final verified outcome.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"appworker-account-created","requirement":"Create the appworker account on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"useradd -m -s /bin/bash appworker succeeded and id appworker resolved to uid=1000(appworker) gid=1000(appworker) both before and after the reboot, confirming the account was created and persisted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bd4ceb840f6348db","cmd-7908558617ca4979","cmd-283aa2e59174468d"]},{"id":"nofile-limit-8192","requirement":"Limit appworker login sessions to 8,192 open files (nofile)","status":"satisfied","summary":"/etc/security/limits.d/appworker.conf sets soft/hard nofile 8192, pam_limits.so is confirmed active in /etc/pam.d/login, and a real login shell (sudo -u appworker -i bash -lc) reports ulimit -n=8192 both pre- and post-reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bd4ceb840f6348db","cmd-b2fb1472bba743f3","cmd-7908558617ca4979","cmd-283aa2e59174468d"]},{"id":"nproc-limit-256","requirement":"Limit appworker login sessions to 256 processes (nproc)","status":"satisfied","summary":"limits.d/appworker.conf sets soft/hard nproc 256; a real bash login session (not the initial sh session, which lacked uli